**Date:** 2026-08-05
**Source:** JumpTask Case Study + HQ Archive
**Tags:** #HumanFactor #Trust #Incentives #Platform #VaultPrinciple

## Observation
Payout dispute with JumpTask: broken links, delayed rewards, generic 72-hour support. Later announced payout overhaul: JMPT retired, credits replace tokens, GIFQ as payout partner, multiple payout methods.

## Pattern
Technology changes. Human nature remains constant. Every digital system eventually encounters human behaviour.
Key drivers: Trust, Hope, Fear, Convenience, Incentives, Decision making.

## Vault Principle
**Simplicity often defeats technological elegance.**
Platforms evolve from token economies to mainstream infrastructure when human friction becomes too high.

